### Bug Description
When I use `fetch_many` to fetch multiple rows of data in MySQL with sqlx pool, after consuming all the data, the connection does not return to pool, and eventually it took all the idle connection available and causing `Error: PoolTimedOut` error when try fetch a new connection.

Here's the code:
```rust

#[derive(sqlx::FromRow, Debug)]
struct Code {
    code: String
}

#[tokio::main]
// or #[actix_web::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), sqlx::Error> {
    let mysql_pool = MySqlPoolOptions::new()
        .max_connections(3) // smaller than n
        .connect("mysql://root:@localhost/test").await?;

    let mut n = 0;

    while n < 5 { // could not fetch connection more than 3, and timeout eventually
        println!("pool size {} idle size {}", mysql_pool.size(), mysql_pool.num_idle());

        let mut stream = sqlx::query_as::<_, Code>("SELECT * FROM codes LIMIT 1").fetch_many(&mysql_pool);

        while let Some(sqlx::Either::Right(code)) = stream.try_next().await? {
            println!("{:?}", code);
        }

        n += 1;
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

**The same code works for Postgres.**

I dig into the source code a bit, found that MySQL executor would yield a `MySqlQueryResult` after consuming the last bit of the result https://github.com/launchbadge/sqlx/blob/main/sqlx-core/src/mysql/connection/executor.rs#L174-L190, so if I change the source code to, it works.
```rust
        while let Some(data) = stream.try_next().await? {
            match data {
                sqlx::Either::Right(code) => println!("{:?}", code),
                sqlx::Either::Left(change) => println!("changes {:?}", change),
            }
        }
```

This seems an inconsistent between MySQL executor and Postgres executor, and I not super sure about the value yield a `sqlx::Either::Left` when eof reached.  I believe if I remove https://github.com/launchbadge/sqlx/blob/main/sqlx-core/src/mysql/connection/executor.rs#L177-L180 it would make implementation more consistent and happy to contribute if this is the case.

### Minimal Reproduction
Provided in above description.

### Info
* SQLx version: 0.6.2
* SQLx features enabled: "runtime-tokio-native-tls", "mysql", "postgres"
* Database server and version: it should cross all mysql version

